<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Thirtieth Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">380 BCE – 343 BCE · capital Sebennytos</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last native Egyptian dynasty, whose temple-building kings held off Persia until Nectanebo II's defeat in 343 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nectanebo-i">Nectanebo I</a>, a general from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebennytos">Sebennytos</a> in the Delta, seized power from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/twenty-ninth-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-ninth Dynasty of Egypt</a> in 380 BCE. In 373 BCE he repelled a large Persian and Greek invasion led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharnabazus-ii">Pharnabazus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iphicrates">Iphicrates</a>, helped by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> flood.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Sebennytic kings were among the greatest temple builders in Egyptian history, with works at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philae">Philae</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnak">Karnak</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edfu">Edfu</a> and the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isis">Isis</a> temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/behbeit-el-hagar">Behbeit el-Hagar</a>. They funded Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> through temple revenues and taxes on trade at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naucratis">Naukratis</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/teos">Teos</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicia">Phoenicia</a> with the Spartan king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agesilaus-ii">Agesilaus</a> but was overthrown by his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nectanebo-ii">Nectanebo II</a>, who ruled for about eighteen years and promoted animal cults.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 343 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxerxes-iii">Artaxerxes III</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nectanebo-ii">Nectanebo II</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pelusium">Pelusium</a>. The king fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a> and probably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>, and the country became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thirty-first-dynasty-of-egypt">Thirty-first Dynasty of Egypt</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. Nectanebo II was the last native <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a>, later turned into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great's</a> father in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-romance">Alexander Romance</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 380 BCE – 343 BCE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:52.14%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>380 BCE – 343 BCE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sebennytos</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nectanebo I, Teos, Nectanebo II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Thirtieth Dynasty, Sebennytic Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-362&amp;focus=thirtieth-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Thirtieth Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5488 1049 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: